    "hypothesis": "For sufficiently large grids, processing 64×64 tiles in anti-diagonal waves exposes independent tiles to OpenMP static work sharing while retaining only tile boundary data and sparse blocked coordinates. This should reduce synchronization relative to cell-level wavefront scheduling and avoid the baseline's quadratic obstacle-storage footprint; smaller grids use the serial rolling-row path to avoid parallel overhead.",
